091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533938 true] [17592186267193 1100 "The points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(-6,-4)$ and $(6,1)$, respectively, and the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a diameter of a circle. Determine the radius $r$ of the circle.\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267193 1113 #uuid "92d71b8d-a6cb-5c28-8e34-cd28a170231b" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267193 1145 "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6-6)^{2}+(-4-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\  & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{13}{2}\n$$" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267194 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267195 13194139533938 true] [17592186267194 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533938 true] [17592186267194 1041 "field-1" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267194 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267195 13194139533938 true] [17592186267194 1110 #uuid "fb79c607-4dfa-5dd4-8799-e9b1843726ea" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267195 1034 "\\frac{13}{2}" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267195 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533938 true] [17592186267195 1111 #uuid "3bab50fa-f609-5d45-a874-88029200b8c0" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267196 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267197 13194139533938 true] [17592186267196 1089 "q-263134" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267196 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533938 true] [17592186267196 1100 "The points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(-3,-4)$ and $(9,8)$, respectively, and the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a diameter of a circle. Determine the radius $r$ of the circle.\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267196 1113 #uuid "f7a2172d-47d5-55a4-bfba-9edbee7bffb4" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267196 1145 "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3-9)^{2}+(-4-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^{2}+(-12)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+144} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{288} \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{12\\sqrt{2}}{2}=6\\sqrt{2}\n$$" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267197 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267198 13194139533938 true] [17592186267197 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533938 true] [17592186267197 1041 "field-1" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267197 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267198 13194139533938 true] [17592186267197 1110 #uuid "a1131fbc-fb07-5469-b1f1-34075ac0a0d3" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267198 1034 "6\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267198 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533938 true] [17592186267198 1111 #uuid "b7ca3d72-eb97-56c8-ae38-8b8fd0c6bc28" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267199 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267200 13194139533938 true] [17592186267199 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267203 13194139533938 true] [17592186267199 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267205 13194139533938 true] [17592186267199 1089 "q-263144" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267199 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533938 true] [17592186267199 1100 "The segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is the diameter of a circle where the points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(-7,2)$ and $(5,-6)$, respectively. Find the coordinates of the center and the radius of the circle.\n\nThe circle is centered at  $(${{field-1}}$,${{field-2}}$)$ and its radius is{{field-3}}." 13194139533938 true] [17592186267199 1113 #uuid "c222bb01-f724-5bcc-bdd1-eb24868f74e2" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267199 1145 "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. So, we can calculate the coordinates of the center using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-7+5}{2},\\frac{2+(-6)}{2}) \\\\  & =(-\\frac{2}{2},-\\frac{4}{2}) \\\\  & =(-1,-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius can be found by calculating the distance between the center $(-1,-2)$ and a point on the circle, such as $(5,-6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-1-5)}^{2}+{(-2-(-6))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{52} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,-2),$ and its radius is $2\\sqrt{13}.$" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267201 13194139533938 true] [17592186267200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267202 13194139533938 true] [17592186267200 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533938 true] [17592186267200 1041 "field-1" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267200 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267202 13194139533938 true] [17592186267200 1110 #uuid "c1169bc1-ab00-54fe-a446-da8d032fa47e" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267201 1034 "1" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267201 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533938 true] [17592186267201 1111 #uuid "a1143a57-d9ca-552f-83b6-95f84afd424c" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267202 1034 "-1" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267202 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533938 true] [17592186267202 1111 #uuid "49105755-7973-5680-931d-5f7905d988c1" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267203 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267204 13194139533938 true] [17592186267203 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533938 true] [17592186267203 1041 "field-2" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267203 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267204 13194139533938 true] [17592186267203 1110 #uuid "1761446f-0215-54a0-883e-15b49b3acb33" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267204 1034 "-2" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267204 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533938 true] [17592186267204 1111 #uuid "169f1da7-4d29-5d14-a805-70664f1a35c5" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267206 13194139533938 true] [17592186267205 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533938 true] [17592186267205 1041 "field-3" 13194139533938 true] [17592186267205 1104 #ed